// extdeps/communication/medium.dag — a recorded means of communication (cited).
//
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Means_of_communication
//
// In the cited "means of communication" framework, a *medium* is the carrier by
// which a sender conveys an idea to a receiver. The framework sorts means by
// transfer type — verbal (speech, telephony), written, screen-oriented, and
// records-transport — and cross-cuts those with natural (speech, gesture: no
// encode step) vs technical (writing, printing, digital: an explicit
// encode -> carry -> decode).
//
// THIS module models one SPECIFIC means: the *recorded / encoded* medium — an
// idea encoded into a carried representation `R`, recovered by a decode whose
// information-preservation is the `fidelity` axis (Lossless | Lossy). That decode
// round-trip is exactly what distinguishes a technical/recorded medium from a
// natural one (speech has no Lossless/Lossy decode of a stored `R`). So `Medium<R>`
// is NOT the framework's universal carrier concept — it is a cited realization of
// one branch of it. That is why it lives in extdeps and not std (§3: the agnostic
// concept stays central; a specific cited realization migrates outward, citing its
// source). The genuinely agnostic carrier (a `Carrier<R>` with no decode/fidelity,
// which this recorded medium would extend) is not modeled yet — no consumer needs
// it; mint it in std only when one does, not by re-coining it here.
//
// Pure model only — no pipeline fold, no Node/RuntimeValue (dsl/std has neither;
// this dsl-tree extdeps module stays equally substrate-free so src/v2 can import it
// cross-tree, exactly as it imports dsl/std).
//
// Layer split (§3):
//   extdeps/communication/medium.dag  — Medium<R> + DecodeFidelity (this file)
//   dsl/std/encoding.dag              — byte-sequence character interpretation lattice
//   dsl/std/fidelity.dag              — TransportClass cost/hermetic axis (unrelated)
//   v2/extdeps/languages/fidelity.dag — per-feature FidelityDisposition<Feature>
//   v2/std/text.dag                   — Unicode text carriers
//
// NAME DISCIPLINE (§3 — SIGNED OFF eager-boar-790 2026-06-18):
//   Types stay `Medium<R>` + `DecodeFidelity`. `Surface`/`Vehicle` rejected
//   (collision / non-standard naming). Do NOT use `Carrier` for THIS type
//   (overloaded: collection backing, text, classification axis, fact-bearing Node —
//   and reserved above for the future agnostic carrier). Do NOT use bare `Fidelity`
//   — collides with extdeps FidelityDisposition<Feature> AND dsl/std/fidelity.dag
//   TransportClass axis. Do not nickname as TextMedium / ByteMedium / StorageMedium
//   (`product.compute_fabric.StorageMedium` is an unrelated product axis).
//   Operator retains pre-merge veto.
//
// FidelityDisposition compose-up (NOT a re-coin): per-feature
// `FidelityDisposition<Feature>` rows (v2/extdeps/languages/fidelity.dag) compose
// UP into medium-level `DecodeFidelity` via a future reduce at the medium-decode
// boundary. This module owns the reduced medium-axis verdict (Lossless | Lossy);
// feature-level dispositions remain in extdeps until that reduce lands.

module extdeps.communication.medium

import extdeps.external_authority { ExternalAuthority }
import extdeps.uri { Uri, Https }

data extdeps_external_authority_anchor: ExternalAuthority = ExternalAuthority {
  uri: Uri {
    scheme: Https
    locator: "en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Means_of_communication"
  }
}

// Whether decoding from a medium back to semantic values loses information.
//
// DECOMPOSITION CHECKPOINT (DESIGN.md §2): 🟢 PRIMITIVE
// Two mutually exclusive decode policies. Consumers `match` on the variant — no
// substrate `is_*` Bool lift (predicate dissolution).
type DecodeFidelity = Lossless | Lossy

// An idea carried in an external medium.
//
// Field ledger (§2 decompress — each field must be genuinely atomic):
//   carried: R — the represented value in this medium instance. Typed by `<R>` so
//     text (R=String), verdicts (R=ProbeVerdict), values, binaries, … share one
//     carrier without a text-flavored `form: String` discriminator (that would be
//     redundant when R=String and would bias non-text media toward stringly encoding).
//   fidelity: DecodeFidelity — whether decode from this medium back to semantic
//     values preserves information for this instance.
//
// DECOMPOSITION CHECKPOINT (DESIGN.md §2): 🟢 PRIMITIVE
// Two atomic axes (carried value + decode policy); no third "kind" field at this layer.
type Medium<R> {
  carried: R
  fidelity: DecodeFidelity
}
